UID:10001438-1790769600-1790775000@nchumanities.org
SUMMARY:Preserving Truth\, Shaping the Future with Merrill Eisenhower Atwater to Benefit the Stan Greenspon Holocaust Education Center
DESCRIPTION:Join us for an inspiring evening with Merrill Eisenhower Atwater\, great-grandson of President Dwight D. Eisenhower\, as he reflects on President Eisenhower’s pivotal role in documenting the horrors of the Holocaust and preserving its history for future generations. Tickets available through Blumenthal Arts Merrill Eisenhower: A Conversation on Memory\, Leadership\, and Legacy | Blumenthal Arts \nMerrill Eisenhower Atwater has embraced his great-grandfather’s legacy as part of his own life’s work. He has become a passionate advocate for Holocaust remembrance and education\, participating in the International March of the Living\, speaking at Holocaust commemorations\, and partnering with organizations dedicated to confronting Holocaust denial and rising antisemitism. \nGuests will also learn how President Eisenhower’s commitment to preserving the historical record continues to inspire efforts by the Stan Greenspon Holocaust Education Center and our partners here in the Carolinas. Welcome – Stan Greenspon Holocaust Education Center \nWe have tickets available for student groups and their accompanying educators at no cost. Please contact terri.eberle@stangreensponcenter.org.
URL:https://nchumanities.org/event/preserving-truth-shaping-the-future-with-merrill-eisenhower-atwater-to-benefit-the-stan-greenspon-holocaust-education-center/
LOCATION:Knight Theater\, 430 South Tryon Street\, Charlotte\, NC\, 28202
CATEGORIES:Humanities Sector Event
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://nchumanities.org/wp-content/uploads/2026/09/Eisenhower-photo.jpg
ORGANIZER;CN="Stan Greenspon Holocaust Education Center":MAILTO:info@stangreensponcenter.org
END:VEVENT
